{{also|Magnolia|magnólia|magnòlia|magnolią}}
==English==
[[Image:Tree dsc00854.jpg|thumb]]

===Etymology===
Named after French botanist {{w|Pierre Magnol}} (1638-1715) {{suffix|en||ia}}. The surname is a form of the male given name ''Magne,'' from {{der|en|la|magnus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌmæɡˈnoʊ.li.ə/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{wikispecies}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[tree]] or [[shrub]] in any species of the [[genus]] ''[[Magnolia]]'', many with large flowers and [[simple]] [[leaf|leaves]].
# The [[flower]] of a magnolia tree.
# A native or resident of the American state of [[Mississippi]].
# A creamy [[white]] colour, like that of some magnolia flowers.
#: {{color panel|F8EDD3}}

